= Questions of Ideology

The SPD has always held many currents of thought. Which one should guide the party for now?

[? if ideology != 0 : We have previously chosen a [+ ideology +] ideology. Changing it will likely have drawbacks. ?]

- @class_struggle: Democratic socialism: we must overcome capitalism, not just manage it.
- @centrist: A modern, pragmatic social democracy of the centre, as Netzwerk Berlin argues.
- @labor: We should work with the trade unions to improve the lives of working people.
- @reform: A Social Democracy of the centre that is fiscally sound, firm on security, and open to the middle classes, as the Seeheimer Kreis argues.
- @easy_discard

@class_struggle
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.ideology && Q.ideology != "left") {
    Q.changed = 1;
}
!}
go-to: changed if changed = 1
on-departure: ideology = "left"; left_strength += 10; linke_coalition += 1; left_dissent -= 5; cdu_relation -= 3; fdp_relation -= 5; nationalization_support += 1; linke_relation += 3

The Parlamentarische Linke and the Jusos want to shift wealth and power, and are open to working with the Linke.

@centrist
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.ideology && Q.ideology != "centrist") {
    Q.changed = 1;
}
!}
go-to: changed if changed = 1
on-departure: ideology = "centrist"; center_strength += 10; center_dissent -= 10; left_dissent -= 5; reformist_dissent -= 5

Netzwerk Berlin wants a modern, open party that can hold the centre ground and still keep the left and the right of the party together.

@labor
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.ideology && Q.ideology != "labor") {
    Q.changed = 1;
}
!}
go-to: changed if changed = 1
on-departure: ideology = "labor"; labor_strength += 10; investment_support += 1; labor_dissent -= 5; linke_relation -= 3

The AfA and the union wing want the party to stay in government to deliver for working people: good wages, secure jobs and public investment.

@reform
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.ideology && Q.ideology != "reformist") {
    Q.changed = 1;
}
!}
go-to: changed if changed = 1
on-departure: ideology = "reformist"; reformist_strength += 10; democratization += 1; reformist_dissent -= 5; cdu_relation += 5; fdp_relation += 5; linke_relation -= 8; moderate_plan_support += 1

The Seeheimer Kreis wants a party of the centre that is trusted on the economy and on security, and is ready to govern with the Union.

@changed
on-arrival: left_dissent += 5; center_dissent += 5; labor_dissent += 5; reformist_dissent += 5

We have changed ideologies. Many in the party feel unmoored.
